messages:
maya: Noticing a large LCP regression for EU users after last night's routing tweak. Charts hang for ~10% of sessions. Trace: https://internal.corp/trace/1767
arjun: SLO view matches. median bootstrap +260ms, p95 ~1.1s. Repro by forcing EU route locally.
ben: quick bundle inspect -> telemetry client ended up in main app shell, pulled via a top-level re-export in src/index. That prevented tree-shaking.
ashley: Confirmed. Telemetry imports locale data for chart labels + heavy helper libs. That added ~30KB gz to the initial payload.
deploy-bot: Canary rollout: service=console-router version=v1.12.3-route-rollout pct=10 started_at=2026-01-12T22:39:00Z
maya: Canary was supposed to be us-west only. New routing fallback allowed EU sessions to hit canary when a pool was constrained. So EU got the bulked bundle.
arjun: Short term options: (A) rollback routing policy (fast), (B) hotfix to lazy-load telemetry (quick PR) + change split rules (safer). Also reduce sampling by default.
ashley: Proposed lazy-init example I put in a draft:
```
// defer telemetry to idle
const initTelemetry = async () => {
  const { startTelemetry } = await import('./telemetry/client');
  startTelemetry({ samplingRate: 0.005 });
};
if ('requestIdleCallback' in window) requestIdleCallback(initTelemetry);
else setTimeout(initTelemetry, 2000);
```
ben: Also adjust bundler split:
```
optimization.splitChunks.cacheGroups.telemetry = {
  test: /[\\/]telemetry[\\/]/,
  name: 'telemetry',
  chunks: 'all',
  priority: 20,
};
```
arjun: Additionally propose gating heavy telemetry features behind an edge-config flag (so we can flip without a router rollout). Edge-config reads are CDN-cached; we'll need a small fallback if config misses.
maya: Edge-config vs config-service discussion: edge-config is async and safer for client toggles; config-service is sync RPC used by router. For rapid toggles we should standardize on edge-config for the console UI flags.
ashley: PR opened: https://code.corp/p/console/+/10022 (lazy-load + splitChunks change + tests asserting telemetry not in app-shell).
ben: Rolling back routing policy now to stop EU traffic to canary. Will notify infra and hold canary until we land the patch.
deploy-bot: Routing policy rollback: service=console-router action=rollback target=eu done_at=2026-01-12T23:05:12Z
maya: After rollback, please monitor LCP, Time to First Contentful Paint (FCP), and chart hang incidents. I'll keep an eye on the observability dashboard for the next 6 hours.
arjun: Follow-ups: 1) land lazy-load + splitChunks (ashley), 2) add edge-config flag + default low sampling (arjun), 3) add lint/CI rule to prevent top-level re-export of telemetry (ben), 4) post-mortem note + checklist item for router rollouts (maya).
ashley: Adding a small unit test to prevent importing telemetry from src/index and a PR description checklist item.
ben: Done with rollback. We'll coordinate a safe re-roll after telemetry chunking lands and we validate SLOs.
maya: Thanks folks. Quick comms note: mark incident as "routing canary -> asset bloat" and link PR/rollback in the incident thread. :thumbsup:
